  "description": "This is a set of rules and code that tells a computer how to make snare drum sounds in a song. Brandon is fixing a mistake so the computer uses the right snare roll note instead of the wrong one.",
  "icon": "music",
  "rawFirstLine": "New standing rule (just captured to memory at\u2026",
  "subtitle": "7d ago \u00b7 89 msgs \u00b7 Home (~/)",
  "blurb": "New standing rule (just captured to memory at `~/.claude/projects/-Users-drwu/memory/feedback_snare_rolls_at_dsharp1.md`):\n\n**Snare rolls go on D#1 / Eb1 (MIDI pitch 39), NOT D1.** D1 (pitch 38) is the main snare HIT. Three rapid D1s give 3 stacked hits, not a roll texture \u2014 the roll sound is the D#1 sample. Default roll-fill pattern is `[D1, D#1, D#1, D#1]` (one accent + three rolls), not `[D1, D1, D1, D1]`.\n\nThis propagates to several places. Please audit and patch:\n\n1. **`~/.claude/skills/drum-realize/`** \u2014 the MIDI realization layer. Look for any fill / roll / pickup generator that emits m",
